ALVA — Combo Assist, Intelligent Move Cancellation, Controller Attack Artwork & Combat Assist Reliability Update

Project and objective

Repository: hiyroscript/alva

Implement a careful, production-quality update to Alva’s combat and controller systems.

This is a gameplay systems update, not a visual redesign or combat-engine rewrite.

The goal is to make combat feel significantly more responsive, allowing players to execute combos naturally, transition between moves intentionally, and consistently benefit from Combat Assist without unexpected cancellations or missed inputs.

There are five deliverables:

1. Add a new Combo assist setting, enabled by default, which intelligently alternates Attack 1 and Attack 2 when the requested attack is on its 0.5-second repeat cooldown.
2. Implement intelligent move cancellation, letting players interrupt their current move with another explicitly requested legal move. Ordinary Run inputs must never cause a cancellation.
3. Display each fighter’s attack artwork beside the corresponding move name in the controller controls editor, matching the existing mobile controls.
4. Fix the bug where holding Run while attacking cancels Combat Assist.
5. Fix the intermittent bug where Combat Assist is ignored when attacking immediately after another move.

All five changes must integrate with one another.

Do not implement them as independent shortcuts that create inconsistencies in the fighter state machine.

